Celecoxib is a substrate of cytochrome P-450 (CYP) 2C9. Poor metabolizers of CYP2C9 should
   start with half the lowest recommended dose and use with caution, or consider alternative
   therapy. Angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors, loop diuretics, and sodium
   phosphates may increase risk for renal dysfunction. Oral corticosteroids, antiplatelet drugs
   (e.g., aspirin), anticoagulants, SSRIs, smoking, alcohol use, older age, and poor health
