Maternal clonazepam use in breast-fed infants: monitor infant for drowsiness, weight gain,
  and developmental milestones. Neonates born to mothers receiving benzodiazepines late in
  pregnancy have experienced symptoms of sedation and/or neonatal withdrawal.
Proposed therapeutic levels (not well established): 20–80 ng/mL. Recommended serum
  sampling time: Obtain trough level within 30 min prior to an oral dose. Steady state is
  typically achieved after 5–8 days continuous therapy using the same dose.
