  nephrotic syndrome, and hypersensitivity reaction (sulfone syndrome). Cholestatic jaundice,
  hepatitis, peripheral neuropathy, and suicidal intent have been reported with systemic use.
Didanosine, rifabutin, and rifampin decrease dapsone levels. Trimethoprim increases dapsone
  levels. Pyrimethamine, nitrofurantoin, primaquine, and zidovudine increase risk for
  hematological side effects.
