Works on CFTR trafficking defects with two correctors (elexacaftor and tezacaftor) and a
  potentiator (ivacaftor). Indicated for individuals with at least one F508del CFTR mutation or
  with CFTR mutations that are responsive based on clinical and/or in vitro data.
Common side effects include headache, URI, abdominal pain, diarrhea, rash, nasal congestion,
  rhinorrhea, rhinitis, influenza sinusitis, and increases in liver enzymes (ALT/AST, bilirubin) and
  serum creatine phosphokinase. Monitor baseline ALT/AST and bilirubin at baseline and repeat
                                                                           Chapter 31       E        975

