  Hypomagnesemia may occur with continuous use and may lead to hypocalcemia and/or
  hypokalemia. Anaphylaxis, angioedema, bronchospasm, acute interstitial nephritis,
  erythema multiforme, urticaria, Stevens-Johnson syndrome, TEN, pancreatitis, and fractures
  of the hip, wrist, and spine (in adults >50 yr old receiving high doses or prolonged therapy
  >1 yr) have been reported. Fundic gland polyps have been associated with long-term use of
  >1 yr.
