Common side effects include GI discomfort, headache, fatigue, rash, and taste perversion.
  Hypersensitivity reactions may result in anaphylaxis, angioedema, severe cutaneous
  reactions, bronchospasm, interstitial nephritis, and urticaria. Prolonged use may result in
  vitamin B12 deficiency (≥2 yr) or hypomagnesemia (>1 yr; sometimes leading to
  hypocalcemia, tetany, arrhythmias, and seizures). Microscopic colitis, resulting in watery
