Contraindicated in poisonings due to phosphorus, inorganic phosphates, or organic phosphates
  without anticholinesterase activity. Do not use as an antidote for carbamate classes of
  pesticides. Removal of secretions and maintaining a patent airway are critical. May cause
  muscle rigidity, laryngospasm, and tachycardia after rapid IV infusion. Drug is generally
  ineffective if administered 36–48 hr after exposure. Additional doses may be necessary.
For IV administration, dilute to 50 mg/mL or less and infuse over 15–30 min (not to exceed
  200 mg/min). Reduce dosage in renal impairment since 80%–90% of the drug is excreted
  unchanged in the urine 12 hr after administration. Severe hepatic impairment may require
  less frequent doses after the initial dose for both IV and IM routes.
